29bb6817-386e-5c6e-b9b4-09a8f5774754" :question/math-academy-id "q-18624" :question/problem "The coefficient of ${x}^{12}$ in the expansion of ${(2+x)}^{15}$ is" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(2+x)}^{15},$ we have $a=2,$ $b=x,$ and $n=15.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+x)^{15}=(\\frac{15}{0}){2}^{15}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{15}{1}){2}^{15-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{15}{2}){2}^{15-2}{x}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{15}{15}){2}^{15-15}{x}^{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{12}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{15}{12}){2}^{15-12}{x}^{12}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{15}{12}){2}^{15-12} & =455\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =455\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =3\\,640.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{12}$ is $3\\,640.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18624/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8de0dd63-23c6-5926-9e33-71e517949af2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18624"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-18627"] :question/problem "The coefficient of ${x}^{7}y$ in the expansion of ${(x+2y)}^{8}$ is" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(x+2y)}^{8},$ we have $a=x,$ $b=2y,$ and $n=8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+2y)}^{8}=(\\frac{8}{0}){x}^{8}(2y)^{0}+(\\frac{8}{1}){x}^{8-1}(2y)^{1}+(\\frac{8}{2}){x}^{8-2}(2y)^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{8}{8}){x}^{8-8}(2y)^{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{7}y$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{8}{1}){x}^{8-1}(2y)^{1}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{8}{1}){x}^{8-1}(2y)^{1} & =8{x}^{7}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =16{x}^{7}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{7}y$ is $16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621/selection/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer/id #uuid "3d65452b-bf9c-5eef-a152-c7471af5d34e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621/selection/26d640514efba3ddcb8c83f76e22a90cad0a8197de8c27af349be5a25d3bb0c2" :answer/id #uuid "ccb44669-6c09-5452-8903-3da761de4065" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,680" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621/selection/422f38974dca0bcd373b73d07f2017a88ccdf0a9447fd9174a576587603d572e" :answer/id #uuid "b7ae7c6f-bf08-5942-8736-6fafbec8d1b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "420" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621/selection/97e373ee96dc53df4ebb943d99bef0c80c1e295b6df17b2d00f1c7d237b26339" :answer/id #uuid "36ea5326-c059-54bb-afdf-108be4f45a70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,040" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621/selection/ddb36cefe45b57cdf20361057f7e592fd2a33452734925b34bffd50f7b380e68" :answer/id #uuid "38612f8d-9461-5cbd-9b3e-9eedb6276689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e9fa98-0a82-59da-8eb3-337bd9e3451a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113621/selection/ddb36cefe45b57cdf20361057f7e592fd2a33452734925b34bffd50f7b380e68" :answer-field/choices ["q-113621/selection/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" "q-113621/selection/26d640514efba3ddcb8c83f76e22a90cad0a8197de8c27af349be5a25d3bb0c2" "q-113621/selection/422f38974dca0bcd373b73d07f2017a88ccdf0a9447fd9174a576587603d572e" "q-113621/selection/97e373ee96dc53df4ebb943d99bef0c80c1e295b6df17b2d00f1c7d237b26339" "q-113621/selection/ddb36cefe45b57cdf20361057f7e592fd2a33452734925b34bffd50f7b380e68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113621" :question/id #uuid "8f5f91ac-3706-5b6e-99d4-de4e4940a4d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-113621" :question/problem "The coefficient of ${x}^{18}$ in the expansion of ${(2+{x}^{3})}^{10}$ is" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(2+{x}^{3})}^{10},$ we have $a=2,$ $b={x}^{3},$ and $n=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(2+{x}^{3})}^{10}=(\\frac{10}{0}){2}^{10}{({x}^{3})}^{0}+(\\frac{10}{1}){2}^{10-1}{({x}^{3})}^{1}+(\\frac{10}{2}){2}^{10-2}{({x}^{3})}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{10}{10}){2}^{10-10}{({x}^{3})}^{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{18}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{10}{6}){2}^{10-6}{({x}^{3})}^{6}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{10}{6}){2}^{10-6}{({x}^{3})}^{6} & =210\\cdot {2}^{4}\\cdot {x}^{18} \\\\  & =210\\cdot 16\\cdot {x}^{18} \\\\  & =3\\,360{x}^{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{18}$ is $3\\,360.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113621/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8de0dd63-23c6-5926-9e33-71e517949af2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113621"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18625/selection/4835b4e43ecabe21a5947e679eb718ce37fea75f7924440029c97e373c0b79f6" :answer/id #uuid "cdd4c87e-a26f-5908-8fa9-2712e35dd3c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\,520" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18625/selection/845cc9e7eafb9cea025bffc4d2f921f4c9550ee01423ef444cf1947d4bc